---
// [WEB-LEGAL-FOLK-1 2026-09-27] /terms rebuilt to the owner-approved mockup
// design/legal-pages/saathum-terms-mock.src.html. OWNER: "exact replica of
// what you have shown me, not an inspired version." Replaces the
// layouts/Content.astro version — same policy text, word-for-word, on the
// new folk shell.
//
// NOTE FOR AI:
//  - Shell + CSS: layouts/LegalFolk.astro (props documented there) + its
//    styles/legal-folk.css. Same conventions as pages/refunds.astro. Do not
//    re-derive the shell here.
//  - This page supplies only content props (title/lead/updated/sticker/toc/
//    prose) — LegalFolk.astro builds the PublicContent SEO object from them.
//  - Prose text below is UNCHANGED from the previous terms.astro (minus the
//    data-i18n/<ui-copy> wrappers) — do not "improve" the wording; this is a
//    shell swap, not a copy edit.
//  - Emails stay plain text "support (@) saathum.com", never mailto.
export const prerender = true;
import LegalFolk from '../layouts/LegalFolk.astro';
import { publicImage } from '../lib/config';
import { BRAND } from '../lib/brand';

const toc = [
  { id: 'status', label: 'Who we are, and where we are in our journey' },
  { id: 'eligibility', label: 'Eligibility & accounts' },
  { id: 'content', label: 'Your content' },
  { id: 'use', label: 'Acceptable use' },
  { id: 'payments', label: 'Payments, payouts & fees' },
  { id: 'shop', label: 'Shop orders (T-shirts)' },
  { id: 'ai', label: 'Artificial intelligence — important disclaimer' },
  { id: 'third', label: 'Third-party services' },
  { id: 'ip', label: 'Intellectual property' },
  { id: 'termination', label: 'Termination' },
  { id: 'disclaimers', label: 'Disclaimers' },
  { id: 'liability', label: 'Limitation of liability' },
  { id: 'indemnification', label: 'Indemnification' },
  { id: 'law', label: 'Governing law' },
  { id: 'changes', label: 'Changes' },
  { id: 'contact', label: 'Contact' },
];
const ganeshImg = publicImage('/assets/bright/ganesh.png', { width: 320, fit: 'scale-down' });
---

<LegalFolk
  title="Terms of Service"
  titleHtml="Terms of <em>Service</em>"
  eyebrow="Legal"
  lead={`The agreement between you and ${BRAND.name} for using ${BRAND.name}.`}
  description={`The agreement between you and ${BRAND.name} — your account, acceptable use, payments, and the limits of what we promise.`}
  image="/og/terms.png"
  updated="2026-10-01"
  sticker={{ src: '/assets/editorial-stickers-v2/terms-sticker-v2.png', width: 1378, height: 1142, alt: 'A red bound book beside a kalash with mango leaves and a diya — terms of service.' }}
  stamp={{ src: '/assets/bright/lotus.png', width: 1254, height: 1254 }}
  toc={toc}
  railCard={{
    title: 'Governed by the laws of India',
    html: 'Read sections 11 and 12 with care — they set out what we promise, and what we do not.',
    image: { src: '/assets/booking/elephant.png', width: 1536, height: 1024 },
  }}
>
  <p>
    These Terms of Service ("Terms") govern your access to and use of the {BRAND.name} websites, apps, and
    services (the "Services"), provided by the {BRAND.name} founding team ("{BRAND.name}", "we", "us", or
    "our"). By using the Services, you agree to these Terms. If you do not agree, do not use the
    Services.
  </p>

  <h2 id="status"><span class="lg-n">1.</span>Who we are, and where we are in our journey</h2>
  <p>
    {BRAND.name} is built and operated by a small team in Dehradun, Uttarakhand, India. Please read
    section 11 (Disclaimers) and section 12 (Limitation of liability) carefully.
  </p>

  <h2 id="eligibility"><span class="lg-n">2.</span>Eligibility &amp; accounts</h2>
  <p>
    You must be able to form a binding contract and meet any minimum age requirements in your
    jurisdiction. You are responsible for your account, for keeping your credentials secure, and for
    all activity under your account.
  </p>

  <h2 id="content"><span class="lg-n">3.</span>Your content</h2>
  <p>
    You retain ownership of the content you create or upload. You grant us a limited, worldwide,
    non-exclusive license to host, store, reproduce, and display your content solely to operate and
    improve the Services. You are responsible for your content and confirm you have the rights to
    share it.
  </p>

  <h2 id="use"><span class="lg-n">4.</span>Acceptable use</h2>
  <p>
    You agree not to misuse the Services — including no illegal activity, harassment, infringement,
    spam, malware, or attempts to disrupt or reverse-engineer the Services.
  </p>

  <h2 id="payments"><span class="lg-n">5.</span>Payments, payouts &amp; fees</h2>
  <p>
    Some features let you earn or spend money. Payments and payouts are handled by third-party
    processors subject to their terms. Applicable fees, revenue shares, and taxes are your
    responsibility where required by law. We may change pricing with notice.
  </p>
  <p>
    If a payment is taken from you in error, tell us at support (@) {BRAND.domain} and we will return
    it. See our <a href="/refunds">Refunds &amp; Cancellations</a> policy.
  </p>

  <h2 id="shop"><span class="lg-n">6.</span>Shop orders (T-shirts)</h2>
  <p>
    {BRAND.name} also sells T-shirts in our shop. These rules apply to every shop order, on top of the rest of
    these Terms.
  </p>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>Printed to order.</strong> Each T-shirt is printed to order for you by our print partner. That is why the size and design you choose cannot be changed once you have paid.</li>
    <li><strong>India only, free delivery.</strong> We deliver within India and nowhere else. Delivery is free: the price you see already includes shipping. It usually takes 5–8 days, and courier delays can happen.</li>
    <li><strong>GST.</strong> GST at 18% is added at checkout on the price (after any coupon), and you see the full total before you pay.</li>
    <li><strong>Paying.</strong> You pay by UPI. Your order is confirmed when we match your payment, and we then send your receipt on WhatsApp and email.</li>
    <li><strong>No returns, exchanges or cancellations.</strong> Printing starts as soon as your payment is confirmed, so we do not accept returns, exchanges or cancellations once an order is paid. This includes a wrong size chosen or a change of mind.</li>
    <li><strong>Wrong or damaged item.</strong> If we send the wrong item, or it arrives damaged, tell us within 48 hours of delivery and include a photo. Use “Wrong item? Report it” on your order in My orders, or email support (@) {BRAND.domain}. We then send a replacement, or refund you in full to the UPI account you paid from.</li>
  </ul>
  <p>
    See our <a href="/refunds#shop">Refunds &amp; Cancellations</a> policy for how a shop refund is paid.
  </p>

  <h2 id="ai"><span class="lg-n">7.</span>Artificial intelligence — important disclaimer</h2>
  <div class="lg-note">
    <div>
      <span class="lg-tag">Please read</span>
      <p>
        {BRAND.name} is an AI-centric product, and some features and content are generated or assisted by
        artificial intelligence. <strong>AI can make mistakes.</strong> AI-generated outputs may be
        inaccurate, incomplete, outdated, or otherwise unreliable, and <strong>{BRAND.name} is not
        responsible or liable</strong> for decisions you make based on them. Always use your own
        judgment and verify important information independently.
      </p>
      <p>
        We have made our best efforts to use imagery generated by AI responsibly. If you come across
        any image or content on {BRAND.name} that you find objectionable, please tell us at
        support (@) {BRAND.domain} and we will review and remove it. Any
        such inclusion was not intentional.
      </p>
    </div>
    <img src={ganeshImg} alt="" aria-hidden="true" width="1254" height="1254" />
  </div>

  <h2 id="third"><span class="lg-n">8.</span>Third-party services</h2>
  <p>
    The Services may link to or integrate third-party products. We are not responsible for
    third-party services, and your use of them is governed by their own terms.
  </p>

  <h2 id="ip"><span class="lg-n">9.</span>Intellectual property</h2>
  <p>
    The Services, including software, design, and trademarks, are owned by {BRAND.name} or its
    licensors and protected by law. These Terms do not grant you rights to our branding except as
    needed to use the Services.
  </p>

  <h2 id="termination"><span class="lg-n">10.</span>Termination</h2>
  <p>
    You may stop using the Services at any time. We may suspend or terminate access if you violate
    these Terms or to protect the Services and our community. Some provisions survive termination.
  </p>

  <h2 id="disclaimers"><span class="lg-n">11.</span>Disclaimers</h2>
  <p>
    The Services are provided "as is" and "as available" without warranties of any kind, to the
    fullest extent permitted by law. We do not warrant that the Services will be uninterrupted,
    error-free, or secure. {BRAND.name} is an evolving product: features may change or be withdrawn with notice.
  </p>
  <p>
    <!-- [WEB-REFRAME-1 2026-09-29] mountain temples: weather and natural events -->
    Rituals are performed at temples in the Himalayas, where snow, landslides, heavy rain and other
    natural events are part of life. They can interrupt live streaming, delay the delivery of your
    video or prasad, or, rarely, force us to reschedule. We will tell you about any such delay on
    WhatsApp and by email. If we cannot perform your ritual at all, you get a full refund as set out
    in our <a href="/refunds">Refund policy</a>.
  </p>

  <h2 id="liability"><span class="lg-n">12.</span>Limitation of liability</h2>
  <p>
    To the maximum extent permitted by law, {BRAND.name}, its founders and its team will not be liable for any
    indirect, incidental, special, consequential, or punitive damages, or for lost profits or data,
    arising from your use of the Services.
  </p>

  <h2 id="indemnification"><span class="lg-n">13.</span>Indemnification</h2>
  <p>
    You agree to indemnify and hold {BRAND.name} and its founders harmless from claims arising out of your content, your
    use of the Services, or your violation of these Terms or applicable law.
  </p>

  <h2 id="law"><span class="lg-n">14.</span>Governing law</h2>
  <p>
    These Terms are governed by the laws of India, without regard to conflict-of-laws
    rules, except where local mandatory consumer-protection laws apply to you. Our contracting entity
    is {BRAND.name}.
  </p>

  <h2 id="changes"><span class="lg-n">15.</span>Changes</h2>
  <p>
    We may update these Terms from time to time. We will post the updated version here and revise
    the "Last updated" date. Continued use after changes means you accept the updated Terms.
  </p>

  <h2 id="contact"><span class="lg-n">16.</span>Contact</h2>
  <p>
    Questions about these Terms? Email support (@) {BRAND.domain} or
    visit our <a href="/contact">contact page</a>.
  </p>
</LegalFolk>
